  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let tangent to parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> is<br /><br /><math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />If equation <math><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is tangent to given circle whose centre is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;then length of perpendicular from centre of circle to equation <math><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to radius of circle.<br /><br />Hence, <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> common tangents are <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> or <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math>",
